## Control {{controlId}}: Supervise Maintenance Activities of Personnel Without Required Access Authorization

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization supervises unauthorized maintenance personnel within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through escorted access procedures and audit logging documented in "Maintenance Personnel Supervision Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**Supervision Requirements:**
- Maintenance personnel without required access authorization (vendor technicians, contractors awaiting clearance) are escorted by authorized personnel at all times during maintenance activities
- All actions performed by supervised maintenance personnel are logged and reviewed
- Supervised sessions use temporary, restricted-scope credentials that are revoked upon maintenance completion
- Physical access to server rooms and network closets requires escort by authorized personnel

{{#if roleAssignmentsConfigured}}
**Authorized Escort Personnel:**
Only personnel with designated administrative roles can escort and supervise unauthorized maintenance staff:
{{#if assignments}}
{{#each assignments}}
- **{{principalDisplayName}}** — Role: {{roleDefinitionName}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if directoryAuditsAvailable}}
**Audit Trail:**
Directory audit logs capture all administrative actions during supervised maintenance sessions, providing attributable records of actions performed.
{{/if}}

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Escort and supervise all unauthorized maintenance personnel; log activities; revoke temporary access upon completion
- **Frequency:** Per maintenance event
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Maintenance Personnel Supervision Policy v1.0, Supervision Log Form MA-006

**Review Frequency:** Per event review; quarterly audit by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine supervision logs, temporary credential records, escort documentation, and audit trail for supervised maintenance sessions.

